  {
    "location": "html-block:7",
    "text": "The PQM II is an ideal choice when continuous monitoring of a three phase system is required. It provides metering for current, voltage, real and reactive power, energy use, cost of power, power factor and frequency. Programmable setpoints and 4 assignable output relays allow control functions to be added for specific applications. This includes basic alarm on over/under current or voltage, unbalance, demand based load shedding, and capacitor power factor correction control. More complex control is possible using the 4 switch inputs which also can be used for status such as breaker open/closed, flow information etc.",
    "heading": "Power Quality Meter"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:8",
    "text": "New In Version 2.10:"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:9",
    "text": "Voltage Disturbance Recorder (VDR) to monitor voltage dips (voltage sags) and voltage spikes (voltage swells) with capacity for 500 sag/swell events.",
    "heading": "New In Version 2.10:"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:10",
    "text": "DNP 3.0 Communications Protocol standard feature.",
    "heading": "New In Version 2.10:"
  },
